OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA cold start, followed by a
OL,6,Fbright and often sunny day. The odd
OL,7,Fshower remains possible, especially
OL,8,Fnear the north and east coasts where
OL,9,Fit will also be rather breezy. Feeling
OL,10,Fchilly.
OL,11,
OL,12,CTonight:FA cold but dry night with
OL,13,Fextensive clear spells allowing a
OL,14,Ffrost to form, particularly in rural
OL,15,Flocations. Coastal spots could still
OL,16,Fsee the odd shower through the night.
OL,17,
OL,18,CFriday:FAnother cold and frosty start,
OL,19,Fwith plenty of sunshine around.
OL,20,FRemaining dry overnight with extensive
OL,21,Fclear spells, allowing a frost to form.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
